    "title": "McDonald's unveils new 'KPop Demon Hunters' meals",
    "text": "FOODMcDonald’s releasing South Korean-inspired 'KPop Demon Hunters' meals Abigail Flores-JohnsonFort Collins ColoradoanUpdated March 31, 2026, 9:18 a.m. MTMcDonald's is having a moment, and it's golden.Inspired by \"KPop Demon Hunters,\" winner of two Oscars in 2026, the global fast-food giant is set to release two new meals themed after girl group HUNTR/X and their rivals, the Saja Boys, on March 31.Each meal lets fans choose a side and comes with a collectible card pack featuring an exclusive photocard from that group, along with a Derpy access card — named after a tiger character in the film. Guests can scan the card’s QR code and enter it in the McDonald’s app by April 26 to unlock exclusive content and a special reveal of the group that wins the ‘Battle for the Fans.’”",
